13. Moderation Logic
Classification and moderation are separate steps. The model estimates label probabilities; the application then derives a score/severity and a suggested action. A typical policy can allow low-risk comments, warn for moderate cases, hide or escalate high-risk cases, and send ambiguous cases for human review. The exact rule thresholds and action mapping must be described from the current implementation rather than invented.
The moderation output is advisory. A model may make false-positive or false-negative predictions, especially for sarcasm, reclaimed language, context-dependent phrases, and rare labels. High-impact actions should include an appeal or human-review process.
