The measured overall element-wise Hamming accuracy is 0.9794 (matching the reported ~0.98), while exact-match subset accuracy is 0.9087. The toxic-label F1-score is 0.8099 (near parity with reported ~0.82). The pos_weight class-balancing mechanism successfully boosted rare-label recall to 83.0% for severe_toxic, 72.5% for identity_hate, and 66.7% for threat.
14.3 Result Interpretation
The evaluation results demonstrate strong ranking discrimination across all six heads with an average ROC-AUC of 0.9903. High element-wise accuracy (0.9794) reflects the natural dataset distribution where ~89.8% of comments contain zero toxicity tags. Exact-match subset accuracy (0.9087) establishes that over 90% of comments have all six binary decisions predicted correctly. Rare-label recall was substantially elevated by the V4 pos_weight weighting, with the expected tradeoff of reduced precision on rare classes.
